      "page": 4,
      "text": "3. Application of the Rules\n\nA violation of the authenticity rules will result in a green card. Depending on the rank of tournament,\ninfraction will be applied differently.\n\nA green card combined with a yellow card will result in a red card and the competitor will be disqualified\nfrom the tournament.\n\nA competitor can receive only 1 green card per tournament, no matter how many infractions they have.\n3.1. Source\n\nNo authenticity check required.\nAuthenticity members on site will be able to give advice and guidance.\n\n3.2. Classic\n\nAuthenticity check is mandatory prior to the start of the tournament.\nA competitor is allowed to enter the list if they respect the following cumulative criterias:\n\n● Have no more than 3 minors infraction (if they have 4 or more, they will receive a green card).\n● Have no more than 1 moderate infraction (if they have 2 or more, they will receive a green card.\n● Have no major infraction.\n\n3.3. Regional\n\nAuthenticity check is mandatory prior to the start of the tournament.\n\nA competitor is allowed to enter the list if they respect the following cumulative criterias.\n● Have no more than 2 minors infraction, if you have 3 or more, then they will receive a green card.\n● Have no moderate infraction. If they have 1 or more, they will receive a green card.\n● Have no major infraction.\n\n3.4. Conference\n\nAuthenticity check is mandatory prior to the start of the tournament.\n\nA competitor is allowed to enter the list if they respect the following cumulative criterias.\n● Have no more than 1 minor infraction, if you have 2 or more, then they will receive a green card.\n● Have no moderate infraction.\n● Have no major infraction.\n\nNote: as an exceptional measure, for season 2025, tournaments of Conference level will be considered\nas Regional regarding Authenticity rules. It means a competitor with 1 moderate infraction will be allowed\nto fight, but will receive a green card.\n\nInfractions Classification and Application V. 26.1] 4/5",
